An interesting idea. Here's my point allocation:
War points
+1 Killing a foe with a weapon.
+200 Angering peacefuls.
-100 pacifying foes (including taming hostiles)
-50 taming peacefuls

Death points
+50 Each time you cast finger of death or zap a wand of death
+150 Each time a creature is killed by your death ray
-200 Each time you turn undead a corpse
-50 each time you polymorph anything into an undead creature.
+10 anytime you poly non-living into a living creature.
-25 for healing anything but yourself.
+10 whenever something dies not to a weapon.

Pestilence points
+20 for using the sickness items mentioned
+50 for using a cursed unihorn
-5 for curing sickness or poison on yourself
+5 for hitting with a poisoned weapon
+50 for killing with poison

Famine points:
+5 for every turn you spend hungry
+25 for every turn spent weak
+50 for every turn spent fainting
-1 for every point of nutrition you consume
-200 for using a horn of plenty.


Naturally these numbers are subject to tweaking, but I think it reflects 
my thoughts on the matter: make the significant events worth a TON and 
some minor-but-constant events worth a lot less. Some more intuitive 
results arise from this system; for example, anyone using a horn of 
plenty is pretty much guaranteed to not become Famine and if you go 
around angering peacefuls you're very likely to become Death.


